MindGrab model weights — provenance and licence
===============================================

`src/mindgrab_weights.c` is generated from the upstream MindGrab checkpoint. The C code that
consumes it (`src/mindgrab.c`, `scripts/export_mindgrab.py`) is niimath's own, BSD-2-Clause
like the rest of the repository; only the 146,237 trained parameters come from upstream.

Artifact
--------
    URL      https://huggingface.co/neuroneural/mindgrab/resolve/main/model.pth
    SHA-256  31f1bda17b8d3eee17a54cf3f199899763a6615a049f05ab2a05f18eb98ec23a
    Config   https://huggingface.co/neuroneural/mindgrab/resolve/main/model.json
    SHA-256  e321f27014eb05f187667873d5301be57f9aac4c5be427e68e9f484748d643fd

Reference implementation: brainchop-cli (https://github.com/neuroneural/brainchop-cli),
MIT, Copyright (c) 2024 spikedoanz (Mike Doan). Validated against brainchop-cli 0.1.24 with tinygrad
(the version installed at validation time; 0.2.x renames the short CLI options but not the model).

Licence
-------
The exact model release above declares `license: mit` in its Hugging Face model-card metadata.
That metadata is the ONLY licence statement that covers these weights, and the whole MIT basis
rests on it. Two things it is worth being precise about:

  * The same bytes are also served from `github.com/neuroneural/brainchop-models`
    (`meshnet/mindgrab/model.pth`), which brainchop-cli still downloads from -- verified
    byte-identical at the SHA-256 above. That repository has NO LICENSE file at all.
  * `neuroneural/brainchop` and `neuroneural/brainchop-cli` are MIT-licensed SOFTWARE
    repositories. They distribute the weights but do not themselves license them, so they are
    not independent confirmation.

The MindGrab paper (arXiv:2506.11860) does not state a licence for the model; the paper itself
is CC BY 4.0. Do not cite it as the licence basis. If upstream ever adds a LICENSE beside the
weights, record it here and this note can be simplified.

